# Logins for the agents in the sandbox.
# Copy this file to .sandcastle/.env and fill in the logins of the agents that
# your factory config uses. Sandcastle passes every variable of .env into the
# sandbox, so do not put other secrets here. Do not add a GitHub token: the
# runner uses the GitHub login of your own machine, outside the sandbox.
#
# Sandcastle passes only the variables that this file lists. If a value here
# is empty, Sandcastle takes it from the environment of the runner.

# Claude Code. Run `claude setup-token` on your machine to get this token. It
# uses your Claude subscription (Pro or Max), not API credits.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Or use an Anthropic API key in place of the token:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Codex. Needed only if a role uses the codex provider.
# Without CODEX_API_KEY, the runner uses your ChatGPT login: it copies
# ~/.codex/auth.json (from `codex login`) into each sandbox. Use an OpenAI API
# key in place of the ChatGPT login:
# CODEX_API_KEY=
